NNAAMMEE
       pam_succeed_if - test account characteristics

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppaamm__ssuucccceeeedd__iiff..ssoo [_f_l_a_g...] [_c_o_n_d_i_t_i_o_n...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       pam_succeed_if.so is designed to succeed or fail authentication based
       on characteristics of the account belonging to the user being
       authenticated or values of other PAM items. One use is to select
       whether to load other modules based on this test.

       The module should be given one or more conditions as module arguments,
       and authentication will succeed only if all of the conditions are met.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       The following _f_l_a_gs are supported:

       ddeebbuugg
           Turns on debugging messages sent to syslog.

       uussee__uuiidd
           Evaluate conditions using the account of the user whose UID the
           application is running under instead of the user being
           authenticated.

       qquuiieett
           Don't log failure or success to the system log.

       qquuiieett__ffaaiill
           Don't log failure to the system log.

       qquuiieett__ssuucccceessss
           Don't log success to the system log.

       aauuddiitt
           Log unknown users to the system log.

       _C_o_n_d_i_t_i_o_ns are three words: a field, a test, and a value to test for.

       Available fields are _u_s_e_r, _u_i_d, _g_i_d, _s_h_e_l_l, _h_o_m_e, _r_u_s_e_r, _r_h_o_s_t, _t_t_y and
       _s_e_r_v_i_c_e:

       ffiieelldd << nnuummbbeerr
           Field has a value numerically less than number.

       ffiieelldd <<== nnuummbbeerr
           Field has a value numerically less than or equal to number.

       ffiieelldd eeqq nnuummbbeerr
           Field has a value numerically equal to number.

       ffiieelldd >>== nnuummbbeerr
           Field has a value numerically greater than or equal to number.

       ffiieelldd >> nnuummbbeerr
           Field has a value numerically greater than number.

       ffiieelldd nnee nnuummbbeerr
